A Bluetooth HID keyboard host on BTstack, Classic and LE: picosdl's
(backend/pico/bt, with ../psdl_pico_log.[ch], its interrupt-safe console
output), BSD-2-Clause as piegpu is, by the same author.

Changed here: the device is called "piegpu"; bt_app tells a screen what it's
doing and which digits pairing wants typed (bt_app_get_status,
bt_app_show_passkey: the two transports call the latter).

btstack_config.h is derived from the pico-examples Pico W Bluetooth
configuration, and kbd_host.gatt follows BTstack's own example, so this
directory carries BSD-3-Clause material:

  Copyright (C) 2009 BlueKitchen GmbH
  Copyright (c) 2020 Raspberry Pi (Trading) Ltd.

BSD-3-Clause adds a no-endorsement clause that BSD-2-Clause does not have: the
names of the copyright holders and of their contributors may not be used to
endorse or promote products derived from this software without specific prior
written permission.

BTstack itself is in the Pico SDK, not distributed here; on Raspberry Pi's
Pico W boards it is used under their licence for it (the SDK's
src/rp2_common/pico_btstack/LICENSE.RP).
